The data tables of this package come from the Unicode Character Database.

The Unicode Character Database files carry the Unicode License. The
license covers the data files and the software of the Unicode
Consortium. The license text is at
https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

The tables are built by the scripts under test/. Each script reads the
files of the Unicode Character Database 17.0.0 and writes numbers only
into the package.

The files of the Character Database that the scripts read:

  UnicodeData.txt
  CaseFolding.txt
  CompositionExclusions.txt
  DerivedNormalizationProps.txt
  GraphemeBreakProperty.txt
  GraphemeBreakTest.txt
  WordBreakProperty.txt
  WordBreakTest.txt
  SentenceBreakProperty.txt
  SentenceBreakTest.txt
  emoji-data.txt
  NormalizationTest.txt
  Scripts.txt
  EastAsianWidth.txt
  DerivedBidiClass.txt
  BidiMirroring.txt
  NumericValue.txt
  SpecialCasing.txt
  DerivedCoreProperties.txt
  Jamo.txt

The UTF-16 test vectors come from the Go, the Node and the Rust
libraries. The UTF-32 test vectors come from the codecs of Python. The
scripts write numbers only. The source code of those libraries is under
the licenses of those projects.

The scripts check each table against a second source. The second source
is the Go standard library, the Go packages golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm,
golang.org/x/text/width and golang.org/x/text/unicode/bidi, the package
golang.org/x/text/cases, the ICU library, Node with ICU and the
unicodedata module of Python. The scripts fail when the sources differ.
The scripts use the unicodedata module as a second check only, because
it holds Unicode 16.0.0.
